{
  "chapter_id": "CH003",
  "title": "Hebrews 2: Death Already Destroyed",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC009",
      "title": "Reading the Text Together",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "We turned together to Hebrews chapter 2, reading it as a group, some in English and some in French. The text declares that Jesus was made a little lower than the angels, and that for the suffering of death we see him crowned with glory and honor. He suffered death for everyone.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA032",
            "SRC000852",
            "SRC000856",
            "SRC000859",
            "SRC000861",
            "REF007",
            "SRC000655",
            "SRC000658",
            "SRC000695",
            "EX004"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000852",
            "SRC000856",
            "SRC000859",
            "SRC000861",
            "SRC000655",
            "SRC000658",
            "SRC000695",
            "SRC000895",
            "SRC000902",
            "SRC000905",
            "SRC000963"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA032"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX004"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF007"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "The passage goes further. Because the children share in flesh and blood, Christ himself likewise shared in the same, so that through death he might destroy the one who holds the power of death, that is, the devil. In French the text was read as saying he passed through death himself in order to act against the one who held that power.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA033",
            "SRC000936",
            "SRC000946",
            "SRC000952",
            "SRC001011",
            "REF007"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000936",
            "SRC000946",
            "SRC000952",
            "SRC001011",
            "SRC000655",
            "SRC000658",
            "SRC000695"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA033"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF007"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "At that point a dispute broke out over the French rendering. The word in question was 'néanti.' One person read it as meaning that the devil was annulled, brought to nothing, destroyed. Another objected that this made it sound as though the devil had only negotiated, retaining some form of power. A third insisted the text says plainly that he was destroyed, and pointed back to the Bible itself as the source of that wording.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA035",
            "SRC000963",
            "SRC000967",
            "SRC000970",
            "SRC000972"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000963",
            "SRC000967",
            "SRC000970",
            "SRC000972"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA035"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC005"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        },
        {
          "text": "That disagreement over the precise force of the French word was not settled in the room, and I leave it exactly as it stood.",
          "kind": "connective",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "UNC005"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000963",
            "SRC000967",
            "SRC000970",
            "SRC000972"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC005"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000004",
          "provider_handle": "p4"
        },
        {
          "text": "We also noted 1 John chapter 3 verse 8 alongside this reading in Hebrews, since both texts speak to the same reality concerning the works of the devil and the purpose of Christ's coming.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "REF008",
            "SRC000674"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000674"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF008"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA032",
        "IDEA033",
        "IDEA035"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC000852",
        "SRC000856",
        "SRC000859",
