        "SRC001011",
        "SRC000967",
        "SRC000970",
        "SRC000972",
        "SRC000674"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC010",
      "title": "The Devil Men Still Boast Of",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "On the Mambila plateau, missionaries went to reach a hill community. The land was given to them by local authority through a ritual involving the throwing of a stone. This part of the account was told to me, and I was not myself present for every detail of how it unfolded.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "EX003",
            "SRC000790",
            "SRC000806",
            "SRC000751",
            "SRC000753",
            "SRC000761",
            "SRC000767"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000790",
            "SRC000806",
            "SRC000751",
            "SRC000753",
            "SRC000761",
            "SRC000767",
            "SRC000820",
            "SRC000750"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX003"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC004"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "After the gospel was preached there, villagers were told to go and take scorpions, and were told that the scorpions would not harm them. They did, and the scorpions did them no harm.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA030",
            "SRC000811",
            "SRC000814",
            "SRC000820"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000811",
            "SRC000814",
            "SRC000820",
            "SRC000790"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA030"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        },
        {
          "text": "I was told something else striking: that it is often the preachers themselves, the very ones who carry the power of God in their life and in their mouth, who end up dodging or trying to escape from exercising that power rather than using it.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA031",
            "SRC000824",
            "SRC000826",
            "SRC000828"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000824",
            "SRC000826",
            "SRC000828"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA031"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a contrast worth naming. If you go to the body of Christ globally, many acknowledge that what they experience of the demonic is comparatively muted. But go to Africa, and you will hear it said that the devils there are real, that the devil in our village is terrible. There is almost a pride taken in how intense the local demonic reality is said to be, set against a global church that speaks of it with far less weight.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA034",
            "SRC000958",
            "SRC001044",
            "SRC001058",
            "SRC001060",
            "SRC001063"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000958",
            "SRC001044",
            "SRC001058",
            "SRC001060",
            "SRC001063"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA034"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000009",
          "provider_handle": "p9"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA030",
        "IDEA031",
        "IDEA034"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC000790",
        "SRC000806",
        "SRC000751",
        "SRC000753",
        "SRC000761",
        "SRC000767",
        "SRC000820",
        "SRC000750",
        "SRC000811",
        "SRC000814",
        "SRC000824",
        "SRC000826",
        "SRC000828",
        "SRC000958",
        "SRC001044",
        "SRC001058",
        "SRC001060",
        "SRC001063"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC011",
      "title": "The Power Is Already Inside",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Many believers carry in their heads an image of a powerful Christ, the one who walked on top of the water. That picture stays fixed as something to admire from a distance, an image of someone else's power rather than something they themselves share in.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA025",
            "SRC000582",
            "SRC000585",
            "SRC000592"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000582",
            "SRC000585",
            "SRC000592",
            "SRC000597"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA025"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000010",
          "provider_handle": "p10"
        },
        {
          "text": "But that power is already inside of you. You do not need to go to any mountain to find it. Greater is he who is in you. The condition is not an external pilgrimage or an extreme discipline; it is already present within.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA026",
            "SRC000597",
            "SRC000600",
            "SRC000603",
            "SRC000605"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000597",
            "SRC000600",
            "SRC000603",
            "SRC000605"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA026"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000011",
          "provider_handle": "p11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Romans chapter 12, verses 1 and 2, instructs that believers are to be presented as a living sacrifice, not conformed to this world but transformed by the renewing of the mind. The battle is fought there, in the mind, and pastors are charged with that renewal rather than with conformity to worldly patterns.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA027",
            "SRC000619",
            "SRC000620",
            "SRC000622",
            "SRC000631",
            "SRC000639",
            "REF005"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000619",
            "SRC000620",
            "SRC000622",
            "SRC000631",
            "SRC000639"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA027"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF005"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000012",
          "provider_handle": "p12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Churches are not to keep handing people another revelation. Teach the same thing. Teach Jesus and him glorified. Do not change.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA028",
            "SRC000646",
            "SRC000649",
            "SRC000650",
            "SRC000651"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000646",
            "SRC000649",
            "SRC000650",
            "SRC000651"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA028"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000013",
          "provider_handle": "p13"
        },
        {
          "text": "You deserve glory. Many resist this and say no, you don't deserve glory, because that is what they were taught. But that refusal is itself antichrist thinking, a false modesty that denies what belongs to the believer the way it belonged to Christ.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA029",
            "SRC000716",
            "SRC000722",
            "SRC000730",
            "SRC000735"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000716",
            "SRC000722",
            "SRC000730",
            "SRC000735"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA029"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000014",
          "provider_handle": "p14"
        },
        {
          "text": "One reference was raised in passing, Romans chapter 10, somewhere around verse 7, though the precise point intended there was not fully developed in what was said.",
          "kind": "connective",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "REF004",
            "SRC000563",
            "SRC000564"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC000563",
            "SRC000564"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF004"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000015",
          "provider_handle": "p15"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA025",
        "IDEA026",
        "IDEA027",
        "IDEA028",
        "IDEA029"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
