        "SRC000639",
        "SRC000646",
        "SRC000649",
        "SRC000650",
        "SRC000651",
        "SRC000716",
        "SRC000722",
        "SRC000730",
        "SRC000735",
        "SRC000563",
        "SRC000564"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC012",
      "title": "Which Gospel Will You Preach?",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The question was put directly: what are you going to be teaching from today? The apostles could each say, my gospel which I brought to you. So what will be your gospel, going forward, now that this has been read and heard?",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA038",
            "SRC001148",
            "SRC001154",
            "SRC001159",
            "SRC001166"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001148",
            "SRC001154",
            "SRC001159",
            "SRC001166"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA038"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000016",
          "provider_handle": "p16"
        },
        {
          "text": "When you have discovered that the devil has been destroyed, and that death is destroyed, imagine what your prayer will be tonight. Discovering this changes the very content and boldness of what you bring before God.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA098",
            "SRC002760",
            "SRC002762",
            "SRC002764"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC002760",
            "SRC002762",
            "SRC002764",
            "SRC002791",
            "SRC002792",
            "SRC002793"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA098"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000017",
          "provider_handle": "p17"
        },
        {
          "text": "A demon can walk into your house and you will not even bother, because you know what that thing is. If the master is destroyed, what is this one? There is a confidence that comes with knowledge. When you know this thing, everybody can run from you. But I know who you are: you are a paper tiger, a bulldog without teeth.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA099",
            "SRC002783",
            "SRC002785",
            "SRC002786",
            "SRC002788",
            "SRC002791",
            "SRC002792",
            "SRC002793",
            "SRC002794",
            "SRC002795",
            "SRC002796"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC002783",
            "SRC002785",
            "SRC002786",
            "SRC002788",
            "SRC002791",
            "SRC002792",
            "SRC002793",
            "SRC002794",
            "SRC002795",
            "SRC002796"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA099"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000018",
          "provider_handle": "p18"
        }
      ],
